hypothesis: >-
  H45 is refuted as stated. The GEMM2 phase of tc_kernel is much shorter than assumed: 1.5 / 3.3 / 7.3 / 14.2 / 3.0 us
  at 2/8/16/32,768 and 8,384. Its 48 KB stages are bound by L2 bandwidth (~109 GB/s/SM on 148 SMs, about 16 TB/s), not
  by MMA issue, so one MMA per [h|g] stage gains nothing. The bulk reduce is only 1.25x faster than scalar red.add, and
  the ~2 us drain tail is set by the reduction bytes (out x KS) that all land at the end. What pays is cutting B bytes:
  at 32,768 each GEMM2 unit covers 256 output channels (MP=2), so two W2 tiles share each landed B stage and phase C
  falls from 16.0 to 11.3 us; that row runs 57.6 vs 61.4 us in run_tests. The other rows move by -0.8 us or less.
