  - "Mechanism: 32,768 moves 288 x 16 x 48 KB = 221 MB of GEMM2 operands in ~14 us, about 16 TB/s, which is the L2 cross-die ceiling. 0.44 us per 48 KB stage is ~57 B/clk/SM: L2 bandwidth, not MMA (one N=256 MMA per k16 instead of two N=128 left the stage time at 0.44 us) [probe_b200]"
  - "STEP 2: cp.reduce.async.bulk.global.shared::cta.bulk_group.add.f32 compiles on sm_100a and is bit-equal to red.add. 148 CTAs x 25 KB into a just-prefilled output: 3.34 / 4.32 / 6.53 us for 1/2/4 tiles per CTA, against 3.52 / 4.77 / 7.5 for the parent's 16-lane scalar red pattern. The marginal rate is ~1.25x better; on a cold output the two are equal (2.8 TB/s, DRAM-bound) [probe_b200]"
