  - "STEP 3(b'), MP=2 (two W2 tiles share one [h|g] B stage, 64 KB 3-deep stages, 2x256 TMEM columns): 32,768 KS 3 (144 units) 59.4-59.5 vs 63.0-63.1 us interleaved; phase C 16.0 -> 11.3 us, mainloop 15.75 -> 10.75. 32,768 KS 6 (2 units per CTA, no TMEM double buffer): 63.4 (worse). 16,768 MP 2 KS 6: 40.75 vs 41.18 (-0.4, reduction bytes double; not shipped). 8,768 MP 2 KS 12: 30.92 vs 30.27 (worse) [probe_b200]"
  - "Drain tail after the last mainloop: 1.75-3.0 us whatever the drain form, about bytes_reduced_at_end / ~4.8 TB/s (32,768 MP=2: 14.5 MB, 3.0 us; MP=1 with 2 units per CTA: 2.0 us, because half overlaps the second unit). The tail falls only if KS (reduction bytes) falls or if the drain overlaps another unit's mainloop [probe_b200]"
  - "run_tests 16/16 PASS (portal-order re-runs included), same GPU as r10-merge (rented us): 32,768 57.6 vs 61.4 (-6.1 %); 2,768 22.8 vs 23.6; 8,768 29.9 vs 30.5; 16,768 40.4 vs 40.4; 8,384 33.8 vs 34.0; 16,384 49.4 vs 51.6 (tc2 code unchanged: that is noise); sc rows -0.7..+0.6 (unchanged code) [run_tests]"
  - "Verdict against the E1 bars: GEMM2 phase >= 40 % shorter on >= 4 rows: missed (only 32,768, -30 %). Row targets: 32,768 -3.7..-3.8 us vs >= 4 (narrow miss); 16,768, 16,384, 8,768, 8,384 and 2,768 missed. Refutation clause fires: bulk < 1.3x scalar in STEP 2 and the shipped build is within 1 us of the parent on 5 of 6 rows. H45 as stated: refuted. Lever kept: B sharing across output-channel tiles (MP=2) where GEMM2 runs >= 16 stages per CTA [run_tests, probe_b200]"
  - "PRECISION: the roundings are unchanged (d16, fp16(lnw*W1), h16, g16, fp16 W2, the GELU); only the fp32 summation order of the split-K partials changes (bulk add vs red.add, MP doesn't change KS at 32,768). Single seed against an fp64 reference with the harness generators, shipped variant: 2,768 1.55e-3 (atol 2.6e-3), 8,768 1.70e-3, 16,768 1.70e-3, 32,768 1.79e-3 (2.9e-3), identical to the parent-equivalent build; outputs differ from it by <= 4e-6. The r8 10-round log (tc 59-65 % of atol) stands [probe_b200]"
  - "Dead ends: one MMA over [h|g] alone (stage time unchanged, L2-bound); ring staging plus wait_group.read (<= 0.5 us); MP=2 at 8,768 and 16,768 (doubled reduction bytes cancel the halved B ingest); MP=2 with 2 units per CTA (no TMEM double buffering) [probe_b200]"
  - "Merge advice: take 32,768 from this kernel (-3.8 us rented, ~-4.5 us portal at D's 1.2-1.3 ratio, about +0.0007 of mean). 2,768 / 8,768 (-0.6..-0.8 us) are noise-level; take them only if an interleaved merge timing confirms. For D r12 the next GEMM2 lever is fewer reduction bytes at the end (lineage J's cluster reduce, or overlapping drains), and GEMM1 phase B (9.5-28 us) is the larger term (lineage K) [INFERRED]"
  - "Pitfalls: probe containers often do not keep /tmp between calls, so embed every source in each probe. A tc_kernel-only .so built with nvcc and called through ctypes builds in ~3 s for 6 variants, against ~20-40 s for a torch extension; that is the fast loop for tc_kernel work. The globaltimer resolution here is ~0.25 us [probe_b200]"
